  "interpretation": "All three predeclared decision-tree contrasts were positive, but their magnitudes were strongly hierarchical. Restoring standing investment variation had by far the largest effect on terminal investment response. Increasing de novo investment mutation supply produced a smaller rescue, about 9.4% of the standing-variation contrast. Increasing plant capacity from 48 to 192 only weakly strengthened mutation rescue. Under this synthetic 400-year experiment, available standing variation is therefore the dominant identified genetic bottleneck, with de novo mutation supply secondary and finite establishment a much smaller modifier.",
